   }
  },
  {
   "id": "an",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 560,
   "y": 440,
   "width": 428,
   "height": 165,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100083,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700581,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A game has ONE row but potentially 80+ moves over its\nlife, each needing its own immutable record - one parent,\nmany children, and the children's write pattern (append\nconstantly, never update) is nothing like the parent's.\n\nKeeping moves separate also means the in-memory\nboard_state a GameSession validates against and the\ndurable log serve genuinely different jobs: one is the\nfast path for 'is this move legal right now', the other\nis the permanent record AND the thing a restarting\ninstance replays to rebuild that fast path from scratch.",
   "originalText": "A game has ONE row but potentially 80+ moves over its\nlife, each needing its own immutable record - one parent,\nmany children, and the children's write pattern (append\nconstantly, never update) is nothing like the parent's.\n\nKeeping moves separate also means the in-memory\nboard_state a GameSession validates against and the\ndurable log serve genuinely different jobs: one is the\nfast path for 'is this move legal right now', the other\nis the permanent record AND the thing a restarting\ninstance replays to rebuild that fast path from scratch.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1130,
   "y": 440,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 120,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100084,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700588,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "board_fen_after is denormalized onto EVERY move row, so reconstructing 'what did\nthe board look like at move 40' never requires replaying moves 1 through 39\nfirst: a spectator jumping to a point in a game, or a post-game review tool,\nreads ONE row.\n\nThe same 'freeze a value that is expensive to recompute' instinct as an\ne-commerce total_amount or a conversation's last_message_at - a small amount of\nstorage now, against an expensive recomputation on every read later.",
   "originalText": "board_fen_after is denormalized onto EVERY move row, so reconstructing 'what did\nthe board look like at move 40' never requires replaying moves 1 through 39\nfirst: a spectator jumping to a point in a game, or a post-game review tool,\nreads ONE row.\n\nThe same 'freeze a value that is expensive to recompute' instinct as an\ne-commerce total_amount or a conversation's last_message_at - a small amount of\nstorage now, against an expensive recomputation on every read later.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
