   "seed": 100088,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700616,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "the rating-bucketed pool          IN MEMORY (or Redis) - never on disk\n    partitioned by time_control FIRST\n        blitz    -> rating buckets -> waiting tickets\n        rapid    -> rating buckets -> waiting tickets\n        classical-> rating buckets -> waiting tickets",
   "originalText": "the rating-bucketed pool          IN MEMORY (or Redis) - never on disk\n    partitioned by time_control FIRST\n        blitz    -> rating buckets -> waiting tickets\n        rapid    -> rating buckets -> waiting tickets\n        classical-> rating buckets -> waiting tickets",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "pool",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 960,
   "y": 656,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100089,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700623,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A ticket's entire life is single-digit seconds - enqueue, get scanned by a\nwidening window, get matched or cancelled - so a durable round trip on every\ntick's scan would be paying a durability cost for data that is cheap to lose AND\ncheap to regenerate.",
   "originalText": "A ticket's entire life is single-digit seconds - enqueue, get scanned by a\nwidening window, get matched or cancelled - so a durable round trip on every\ntick's scan would be paying a durability cost for data that is cheap to lose AND\ncheap to regenerate.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 960,
   "y": 736,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100090,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700630,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "If a pool node crashes, the practical outcome is that a handful of waiting\nplayers' clients notice their ticket vanished and re-issue the queue request: a\nsafe, cheap redo, nothing like losing a move or a rating update.",
   "originalText": "If a pool node crashes, the practical outcome is that a handful of waiting\nplayers' clients notice their ticket vanished and re-issue the queue request: a\nsafe, cheap redo, nothing like losing a move or a rating update.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 806,
   "width": 1027,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100091,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700637,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A blitz player must never be matched from a classical-only rating pool, which is why TIME CONTROL is the primary partition with\nthe rating-bucket structure nested inside it. And a single wildly popular time control - blitz, usually - can be split further\nby a rating-band sub-hash if one partition's scan volume outgrows a node.",
   "originalText": "A blitz player must never be matched from a classical-only rating pool, which is why TIME CONTROL is the primary partition with\nthe rating-bucket structure nested inside it. And a single wildly popular time control - blitz, usually - can be split further\nby a rating-band sub-hash if one partition's scan volume outgrows a node.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d3",
