  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 942,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 162,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100094,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700658,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "moves(game_id, ply_number)              COMPOSITE: the single most common read in the system ('this game's moves, in order')\n                                        and simultaneously the idempotency backstop against a duplicate append for one ply\ngames(status, ended_at)                 the abandonment-timer sweep and any reconciliation job: 'games stuck active past their\n                                        expected end' - the same shape as the payments reconciliation index and the job\n                                        scheduler's due-jobs index\ngames(player_white_id, started_at)      a player's own game history, most-recent-first: the query every profile page runs.\ngames(player_black_id, started_at)      TWO indexes, because a player can be either colour and neither index covers the other.\nplayers(rating)                         seeds the rating-bucketed pool at process start or after a full restart, AND serves\n                                        the 'top rated players' read path\nrating_history(player_id, applied_at)   'this player's rating over time' - the query a profile's rating graph runs",
   "originalText": "moves(game_id, ply_number)              COMPOSITE: the single most common read in the system ('this game's moves, in order')\n                                        and simultaneously the idempotency backstop against a duplicate append for one ply\ngames(status, ended_at)                 the abandonment-timer sweep and any reconciliation job: 'games stuck active past their\n                                        expected end' - the same shape as the payments reconciliation index and the job\n                                        scheduler's due-jobs index\ngames(player_white_id, started_at)      a player's own game history, most-recent-first: the query every profile page runs.\ngames(player_black_id, started_at)      TWO indexes, because a player can be either colour and neither index covers the other.\nplayers(rating)                         seeds the rating-bucketed pool at process start or after a full restart, AND serves\n                                        the 'top rated players' read path\nrating_history(player_id, applied_at)   'this player's rating over time' - the query a profile's rating graph runs",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
